2 NOTE This is not a drawing but a picture of an old statue from the second church in Veteli parish. The original is to be found in Veteli museum. It is said that it is a depiction of Saint Christophoros, or of the first inhabitant of th
3 CONC e parish, or Kauppi Ollinpoika Torppa. My guess is that all three things are true. Nobody knows what the saint looked like, nor does anybody know who the first inhabitant was or what he looked like. But Kauppi Ollinpoika Torppa wa
3 CONC s presumably alive when the statue was made, or at least the sculptor knew what he looked like and made the statue to look like him.
3 CONT It was not uncommon to make statues and pictures to look like contemporary people known to the artist. 
2 NOTE Please tell me where this drawing is from and who is depicted in it?
